CHANGES SINCE VERSION 0.933

-- 2002.03.01 ET:

-----------------------------------------------------------------------

-----------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Numerous trivial bug fixes.

2. Numerous improvements and corrections to the documentation.

3. The TabDelimited output format is now documented.

4. The CommaDelimited, SpaceDelimited, and TabDelimited generic output
   formats now correctly handle date variables.  Dates are written
   out in YYYY-MM-DD format.  Space-delimited files with dates in 
   YYYY-MM-DD format can be read without ambiguity back into Madeline v.0.935.
   Tab-delimited files produced by Madeline can be quickly imported
   into popular databases such as MySQL (i.e. "LOAD DATA INFILE" command 
   in MySQL).  
   
5. Output of the VIEW DISTINCT VALUES command now shows percentages and
   totals for non-missing and missing values:
   
      M>view distinct values of 18,9,sex
      
      18. D12S1723 has 16 levels:
      
      Level  Value   Cases Percent
      ------ -----   ----- -------
          1. 203/209     1    0.3
          2. 203/211     1    0.3
          3. 205/207     1    0.3
          4. 205/209    10    3.0
          5. 205/211     3    0.9
          6. 205/215     2    0.6
          7. 205/217     1    0.3
          8. 207/211     3    0.9
          9. 209/209    26    7.9  -
         10. 209/211     7    2.1
         11. 209/215    12    3.6
         12. 209/217     3    0.9
         13. 211/211     6    1.8
         14. 211/215     2    0.6
         15. 211/217     1    0.3
         16. 215/215     1    0.3
      ------ -----   ----- -------
          .. .......    80   24.2   non-missing values in database
          .. .......   251   75.8       missing values in database
      
      9. CAFFECTED has 4 levels:
      
      Level  V Cases Percent
      ------ - ----- -------
          1. A   134   40.5  -+-+-+-+
          2. D    40   12.1  -+
          3. I    70   21.1  -+-+
          4. U    87   26.3  -+-+-
      ------ - ----- -------
          .. .   331  100.0   non-missing values in database
          .. .     0    0.0       missing values in database
      
      3. SEX has 2 levels:
      
      Level  V Cases Percent
      ------ - ----- -------
          1. F   170   51.4  -+-+-+-+-+
          2. M   161   48.6  -+-+-+-+-
      ------ - ----- -------
          .. .   331  100.0   non-missing values in database
          .. .     0    0.0       missing values in database
      

6. A bug related to aggregate function processing has been 
   fixed.  I doubt if anybody beside me ever encountered 
   this bug which was as follows:
   
   Suppose the case of a mother with 3 affected offspring
   (coded using "A" in the AFFECTED column).  
   Then, by the commutative property, both of the following
   statements should have been true:
   
   OffspringCountTrue( affected="A" ) = 3
   3 = OffspringCountTrue( affected="A" )
   
   ... but it turned out that the first one above would return
   a garbled response due to a bug in the meshwork between
   aggregate function processing and the expression parser.

   This bug has now been squashed out!

   
7. More intelligible names have been given to a number individual
   attributes and  aggregate functions, and new aggregate functions 
   have been added as well.  See the tables toward the end of the
   HTML documentation for a complete treatment:
   
   Individual Attributes     Aggregate Functions
   ---------------------     -------------------
   _NumberOfOffspring        _OffspringCountTrue( <log. expr.> )
   _NumberInPedigree         _OffspringMean( <variable> )
   _IsInDatabase             _OffspringMaximum( <variable> )
   _WasIncluded              _OffspringMinimum( <variable> )
   _MarkedForExclusion       ... etc. ...

  
8. Numeric constants now all begin with the pound character, "#".
   Previously, a number of numeric constants were identified by
   a leading underscore character, "_", such as in "_true" and 
   "_affected", while some others, such as "missing" and "pi", did 
   not even begin with an identifying underscore.  
   
   Since attributes of an individual, such as "_NumberOfOffspring" 
   also began with an underscore character, numeric constants which
   began with an underscore could easily be mistaken for attributes.
   Take "_affected" for example -- was it a constant whose value was
   always 1, or an attribute whose value varied with the individual?
   
   Things should be clear now, as all numeric constants now
   begin with the pound character, "#":
            
            #AFFECTED   
            #ALIVE              
            #DEAD               
            #E               
            #FALSE              
            #FEMALE             
            #MALE             
            #MISSING            
            #P                
            #TRUE          
            #UNAFFECTED         

   Note: This change could affect scripts that you previously wrote.


9. Madeline now actively handles genotypes where only one allele
   has been typed, i.e. "128/0" or "0/137".  See the HTML documentation
   for details.


10. Bug in the GO command that caused the program to exit() when a record
    request was out of range has been fixed.
    
11. Madeline now has an Associative Array data container type to allow
    much more flexible mapping of input values for Affection Status and
    other key attributes.

